{
 "description": "Primitive observation relation declarations for the differential observation judge v1 (Lane A): one receipt directory written by one check harness that put the same pre-registered scenario set to an incumbent implementation and a candidate implementation, and the reviewer rows and admissions that bind it. No model relation is declared here and no model producer class is admitted, so a model row cannot be ingested at all: the claim these relations support is model-free by construction, not by omission. Merge with the derived declarations of rules-observation-v1.json before bundle validation. Two primitives of the spec's original numbering are deliberately NOT declared: P10 observation_effect (one row per persisted effect) and P31 observation_effect_rows_closed (its completeness witness). The unit of effect comparison is effects_digest, which the exporter recomputes from the receipt's effect rows before any row is exported (R-3) and which effects_disagree compares; a row-level relation could only restate that at finer grain, no rule read either, and a declared primitive nothing reads is coverage-shaped dead weight. The receipt's effects rows and its completeness.by_side.<side>.effect_rows box are unchanged on the wire: the rows stay the evidence for the digest, checked at ingest, and an open effect_rows box is still disclosed in the exporter's messages. The spec's P-numbers above P10 are therefore offset by one and above P31 by two in this declaration set.",
